{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01URtS7cxgk2HbLesBPKFV3X","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! C variadic entry points.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Defining `extern \"C\"` variadic functions is still unstable in Rust, so the\n4\t//! six variadic symbols exported by libjansson are implemented as naked\n5\t//! functions containing hand written x86-64 System V trampolines.  Each one\n6\t//! materialises a `va_list` (`__va_list_tag`) on the stack exactly the way\n7\t//! `va_start` does and forwards to the corresponding `v*` function implemented\n8\t//! in Rust.\n9\t//!\n10\t//! Stack frame used by every trampoline (`rbp` is 16-byte aligned on entry):\n11\t//!\n12\t//! ```text\n13\t//!   rbp+16 .. : incoming stack arguments  (overflow_arg_area)\n14\t//!   rbp-176   : register save area, 6 GP quadwords then 8 XMM oct-words\n15\t//!   rbp-208   : the __va_list_tag itself\n16\t//! ```\n17\t//!\n18\t//! `gp_offset` is initialised to `8 * <number of fixed integer arguments>` and\n19\t//! `fp_offset` to 48 (no function below takes a fixed floating point\n20\t//! argument), matching what GCC's `va_start` produces.\n21\t\n22\tuse crate::types::{json_error_t, json_t};\n23\tuse core::arch::naked_asm;\n24\tuse core::ffi::{c_char, c_int};\n25\t\n26\t/* --------------------------------------------------------- jsonp_error_set */\n27\t\n28\t/// `void jsonp_error_set(json_error_t *, int, int, size_t, enum, const char *, ...)`\n29\t#[cfg(target_arch = \"x86_64\")]\n30\t#[unsafe(naked)]\n31\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n32\tpub unsafe extern \"C\" fn jsonp_error_set(\n33\t    _error: *mut json_error_t,\n34\t    _line: c_int,\n35\t    _column: c_int,\n36\t    _position: usize,\n37\t    _code: c_int,\n38\t    _msg: *const c_char,\n39\t) {\n40\t    naked_asm!(\n41\t        \"pushq %rbp\",\n42\t        \"movq %rsp, %rbp\",\n43\t        \"subq $240, %rsp\",\n44\t        \"movq %rdi, -176(%rbp)\",\n45\t        \"movq %rsi, -168(%rbp)\",\n46\t        \"movq %rdx, -1