{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xm3fv5h3a47q6ahrhcg3xkaq76h2ukipiygyfbwcawkmlkm2i2rq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## What was verified\n\n**Library:** jansson 2.15.0 (13 C files, ~13 kLOC C → ~11 kLOC Rust), one build configuration.\n\n### Phase A — artifacts (all in the crate root)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | generated mechanically by `gen_symbols.sh` from `nm -D`: **130 C symbols / 130 Rust symbols, 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 imported-instead-of-defined** |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **300 rows** — every `return -1` / `return NULL` guard, every `error_set`/`set_error`/`jsonp_error_set` branch, every range/NULL/min-max check, plus a table of all 11 `assert()`s with proofs of unreachability |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **132 rows** — encode/decode/pack flags, allocator modes, all 6 sinks × 6 sources, input shapes at every growth/rehash/depth boundary, locale and hash-seed axes |\n\n### Phase B/C — 110 tests, ~2.0 M compared observations (~180 MB of transcript)\n\nEvery test loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and compares byte-for-byte, including the whole 248-byte `json_error_t` (so error *codes*, not just \"both failed\"). OOM branches are covered by an `oom_sweep` helper that fails allocation *k* for every reachable *k*.\n\n### Real divergences found and fixed (C is always right)\n\n1. **`src/dump.rs`** — `do_dump`/`dump_indent`/`dump_string` did `dump.unwrap()` *before* emitting anything. C only dereferences the callback at each emission point, so `json_dump_callback(json, NULL, …)` returns `-1` in C for a NULL `json`, an out-of-range type tag, a detected cycle, or `JSON_EMBED` on an empty container — Rust aborted. Added a lazy `dump_call()` used by all 24 emission points.\n2. **`src/memory.rs`** — same class: `DO_MALLOC.unwrap()` / `DO_FREE.unwrap()` panicked when a caller installed NULL allocator hooks.\n3. **`src/version.rs` + `Cargo.toml`** — `jansson_version_cmp(INT_MIN,…)` used checked subtraction (panics under `debug-assertions`), and `dtoa.rs` relies on C's wrapping unsigned arithmetic. Fixed with `wrapping_sub` plus `overflow-checks = false` in `[profile.dev]`/`[profile.test]` so every profile has C's arithmetic semantics.\n\n### Phase D — completion gate\n\n- `nm -D` diff is **empty** (independently re-checked outside the script).\n- All 132 `CONFIGS.md` rows and all 300 `ERRORS.md` rows are `[x]`; the three rows that are unreachable by construction (dead `key_len` overflow check, shadowed `\"NULL object value\"` message, `utf8_check_string(ptr, SIZE_MAX)`) are documented with the reason rather than faked.\n- `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`**, so there is exactly one combination; `verify.sh` enumerates the power set anyway and runs `cargo check --all-targets`, `cargo build --release`, symbol parity and `cargo test` for each.\n- Bonus: the whole suite also passes against the **debug** `.so` (`JANSSON_RUST_SO=…/target/debug/libjansson.so RUST_MIN_STACK=…`), which is how findings 3 was caught.\n\n`bash verify.sh` → **ALL GREEN** (110 passed, 0 failed). Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1141,"cache_read_input_tokens":513458,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1141,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4cf60c4-25a5-4fee-b0fc-0b215e8b9320","uuid":"b8cebba3-ee4e-4d23-a4f8-83c44ab6c9bf","timestamp":"2026-08-22T18:57:36.102Z"}
